From 92c344255b48507d354a9eecc5586575bf27cbf8 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: dixonSolutions <203963471+dixonSolutions@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Wed, 21 Oct 2026 21:57:04 +1100
Subject: [PATCH 14/18] ufs: exynos: Do not switch the controller to FMP PRDT
 entries

exynos_ufs_fmp_init() makes the SMC that sets DESCTYPE 3 (128-byte PRDT
entries) but U-Boot keeps 16-byte entries, and the setting outlives
U-Boot: a Linux kernel without UFS inline encryption then reads every
multi-entry PRDT at the wrong stride and the controller faults on the
bus (IS.SBFES). Seen on the Galaxy Tab Active3 (Exynos9810) booting
Duranium through EFI. Only do it with CONFIG_UFS_EXYNOS_FMP.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
---
 drivers/ufs/ufs-exynos.c | 12 +++++++++++-
 1 file changed, 11 insertions(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/drivers/ufs/ufs-exynos.c b/drivers/ufs/ufs-exynos.c
index ce65b47f..80318543 100644
--- a/drivers/ufs/ufs-exynos.c
+++ b/drivers/ufs/ufs-exynos.c
@@ -996,7 +996,17 @@ static int exynos_ufs_init(struct ufs_hba *hba)
 
 	exynos_ufs_priv_init(hba, ufs);
 
-	exynos_ufs_fmp_init(hba, ufs);
+	/*
+	 * Not exynos_ufs_fmp_init(): its SMC switches the controller to the
+	 * 128-byte FMP PRDT entries (DESCTYPE 3) for good, while U-Boot keeps
+	 * using standard 16-byte entries, and so does the OS kernel after us
+	 * unless it enables inline encryption. Linux then gets garbage DMA
+	 * addresses from every multi-entry PRDT (System Bus Fatal Errors).
+	 * U-Boot does not use inline encryption, so leave FMP as the previous
+	 * bootloader set it.
+	 */
+	if (IS_ENABLED(CONFIG_UFS_EXYNOS_FMP))
+		exynos_ufs_fmp_init(hba, ufs);
 
 	if (ufs->drv_data->drv_init) {
 		ret = ufs->drv_data->drv_init(ufs);
-- 
